 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Not rude at all. Many restaurants expect that, so you' usually get it before the food comes. Most places today expect you to do that online first and just call for the tip. It saves both sides waiting. A 15% tip for a big group is about right. It adds up quickly, especially on dinners with several courses. You did the right thing. It shows you appreciate service, and it means the waitstaff can keep everyone getting water and menus without waiting for tips.",
